# Environment variables the reference app reads at startup (ConfigFromEnv in
# internal/app/server.go and the app-level reads in internal/app/*.go) -- every
# value is read with os.Getenv, so this file is a reference for what to set,
# not something the app loads itself (there is no dotenv loader in this
# codebase; apply it with your shell or process manager, e.g.
# `env $(cat .env | xargs) go run ./cmd/server`).
#
# Generated from the same table that feeds docs/config-reference.md's bootstrap
# section by examples/reference-app/cmd/configrefgen; a key the app reads but
# this file lacks fails the generator's drift gate. The six key-material rows
# are also declared by the platform modules that consume them (see the
# reference's per-module section), and the generator fails when the
# declaration and the row disagree. Every variable is OPTIONAL: each falls
# back to the documented development default in the comment below, so
# `go run ./cmd/server` with none of this set boots a working standalone
# server. Copy this file to .env, fill in what you need, and never commit the
# real .env (see the repository's .gitignore). Secret materials (marked below)
# must come from a secret store in a real deployment.


# --- Core bootstrap ---
# SQLite database file path (relative to the working directory). Unset fallback: reference-app.db.
APP_DB_PATH=reference-app.db
# Deployment topology: standalone (default) or distributed; constrains which seam implementations may compose. Unset fallback: standalone.
APP_DEPLOYMENT_MODE=standalone
# HTTP listen port. Unset fallback: 8080.
PORT=8080

# --- Key materials (each a hex-encoded 32-byte key; recommended: set APP_ROOT_KEY alone) ---
# HMAC key authn indexes users.email_index/phone_index with; must stay identical across restarts or stored indexes become unfindable. (SECRET) Unset fallback: documented non-secret development default.
APP_AUTHN_BLIND_INDEX_KEY=
# AES key sealing authn's encrypted PII columns (email, phone, TOTP secrets); separate from every other key. (SECRET) Unset fallback: documented non-secret development default.
APP_AUTHN_PII_CIPHER_KEY=
# Master key the config module seals every Sensitive dynamic-configuration value with; the key that encrypts the configs table can never live in that table. (SECRET) Unset fallback: documented non-secret development default.
APP_CONFIG_KEY=
# HMAC key the notification module's blind indexers index encrypted contact addresses with; separate from every other key. (SECRET) Unset fallback: documented non-secret development default.
APP_NOTIFICATION_INDEX_KEY=
# HMAC key org's blind indexer indexes invitation email addresses with; separate from APP_CONFIG_KEY (an AES key must never double as an HMAC key). (SECRET) Unset fallback: documented non-secret development default.
APP_ORG_INDEX_KEY=
# AES key sealing go/pki's LocalSigner private-key column, the key authn's access tokens are ultimately signed with. (SECRET) Unset fallback: documented non-secret development default.
APP_PKI_LOCAL_KEY_CIPHER_KEY=
# Single root secret from which the other six keys of this group are derived (HKDF-SHA256, one purpose string per key); an explicitly-set individual key always wins over its derivation. (SECRET) Unset fallback: individual development defaults.
APP_ROOT_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_64_HEX_CHARS

# --- Infrastructure seams (leave unset to keep the zero-setup standalone defaults) ---
# Fixed local directory for the objectstore seam, the SurvivesRestart twin of the S3 composition; setting both is refused. Unset fallback: throwaway temp directory.
APP_OBJECT_STORE_ROOT=
# Redis address composing real, multi-replica-safe EventBus and KVStore implementations for both seams. Unset fallback: in-process eventbus/kv (Preset default).
APP_REDIS_ADDR=localhost:6379
# S3 access key id for the objectstore seam (required with the S3 group). Unset fallback: local-directory objectstore (Preset default).
APP_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3 bucket name for the objectstore seam (required with the S3 group). Unset fallback: local-directory objectstore (Preset default).
APP_S3_BUCKET=
# S3-compatible endpoint; required together with bucket/access-key/secret-key below. Unset fallback: local-directory objectstore (Preset default).
APP_S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# Optional S3 region, used only when the S3 group above is set. Unset fallback: unset (ignored by S3-compatible local servers).
APP_S3_REGION=
# S3 secret key for the objectstore seam (required with the S3 group). (SECRET) Unset fallback: local-directory objectstore (Preset default).
APP_S3_SECRET_KEY=
# Whether the S3 endpoint speaks TLS (optional; plain HTTP is the local-server default). Unset fallback: false.
APP_S3_USE_SSL=false
# Endpoint the real HTTP SMS transport posts delivery requests to; the URL is where gateway credentials live. (SECRET) Unset fallback: console SMS sender (standalone) / refused boot (distributed).
APP_SMS_GATEWAY_URL=
# SMTP host composing a real Mailer for the mailer seam; required together with APP_SMTP_PORT. Unset fallback: console mailer (Preset default).
APP_SMTP_HOST=
# Optional SMTP AUTH password. (SECRET) Unset fallback: no SMTP AUTH (optional).
APP_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP port for the mailer seam (required with APP_SMTP_HOST). Unset fallback: console mailer (Preset default).
APP_SMTP_PORT=
# Optional SMTP AUTH username; AUTH activates only when a username is set. Unset fallback: no SMTP AUTH (optional).
APP_SMTP_USERNAME=

# --- Observability ---
# OTLP/gRPC endpoint traces and metrics are pushed to; empty keeps go/observability's local exporters. Unset fallback: local exporters (stdout traces/metrics).
APP_OTLP_ENDPOINT=localhost:4317
# This deployment's own public origin, the base URL outbound mail links render when a tenant has no branded host; an unset value ships mail with unreachable localhost links. Unset fallback: http://localhost:<resolved PORT>.
APP_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=

# --- Client-address trust ---
# Declares the proxy is Fly's, authorizing authn to read the single-hop Fly-Client-IP header; only takes effect alongside APP_TRUSTED_PROXIES ('true' with an empty proxy list refuses boot). Unset fallback: false.
APP_READ_FLY_CLIENT_IP=false
# Comma-separated reverse-proxy addresses this deployment receives requests through; what lets session/login-history records carry the real client address. Unset fallback: no trusted proxies (direct connection address recorded).
APP_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# --- Frontend serving ---
# Directory the server serves the app's built frontend from; unset serves no frontend at all. Unset fallback: no frontend served (API only).
APP_WEB_DIST=

# --- Demo and test rigs ---
# Key the images endpoint accepts; the demo value is not a secret (a local or CI-only fake provider accepts it), while a real deployment's key travels the same variable. Unset fallback: no image credential row written.
APP_AI_GATEWAY_IMAGE_API_KEY=
# Base URL of the OpenAI-compatible images endpoint the smile-simulation pipeline posts to; set together with the API key pair. Unset fallback: no image credential row written.
APP_AI_GATEWAY_IMAGE_BASE_URL=
# Gates the boot-time seed of demo-platform-staff@example.com, the rbac.SystemDomain platform administrator; deliberately separate from APP_DEMO_USERS_PASSWORD. Unset fallback: no platform-staff seed.
APP_DEMO_PLATFORM_STAFF_PASSWORD=
# Gates the boot-time seed of the three demo user accounts (demo-owner/demo-reader/demo-acme-only); a passphrase only a disposable demo server should carry. Unset fallback: no demo-account seed.
APP_DEMO_USERS_PASSWORD=
# Kill switch closing the X-Demo-User/X-Demo-User-Id privilege-escalation hole: any non-empty value makes every route resolve its actor from the verified access token alone. Unset fallback: demo identity headers read (any non-empty value disables them).
APP_DISABLE_DEMO_USER_HEADER=
# Test-only: any non-empty value skips standaloneQueue.Start, so this replica never claims or executes a job itself (the distributed-mode integration proof's other-replica driver). Unset fallback: queue worker started.
APP_DISABLE_QUEUE_WORKER=
# Test-and-e2e-only failure injection: a positive N fails the first N self-service provisioning attempts of each account; anything that is not a non-negative whole number refuses boot. Unset fallback: 0 (disabled).
APP_FAIL_SELF_SERVICE_PROVISION=0
